WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.334
Production security is often about
removing development assumptions.

2
00:00:05.414 --> 00:00:09.694
Express applications may expose verbose
errors, debug routes,

3
00:00:09.774 --> 00:00:14.766
development middleware, permissive
settings, internal documentation,

4
00:00:14.846 --> 00:00:20.235
health details, or metrics that are useful
locally but inappropriate for public

5
00:00:20.315 --> 00:00:22.138
production environments.

6
00:00:22.218 --> 00:00:28.003
Environment-specific configuration should
be explicit, reviewed, and documented.

7
00:00:28.083 --> 00:00:33.710
A setting should not be safe by accident
only because the current deployment happens

8
00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:34.503
to hide it.

9
00:00:34.583 --> 00:00:40.051
Security headers can reduce browser-side
risks when configured appropriately.

10
00:00:40.131 --> 00:00:43.776
Helmet-style middleware can help set
common headers,

11
00:00:43.856 --> 00:00:47.502
but headers still need
application-specific review.

12
00:00:47.582 --> 00:00:52.178
Content Security Policy, framing controls,
content type behavior,

13
00:00:52.258 --> 00:00:57.489
referrer behavior, and transport security
settings all interact with how the

14
00:00:57.569 --> 00:01:02.957
application renders pages, serves static
assets, uses third-party resources,

15
00:01:03.037 --> 00:01:04.622
and handles redirects.

16
00:01:04.702 --> 00:01:09.299
Headers are a useful layer, not proof that
the application is secure.

17
00:01:09.379 --> 00:01:14.292
Express applications often run behind
reverse proxies, load balancers,

18
00:01:14.372 --> 00:01:17.938
TLS termination points, or platform
routing layers.

19
00:01:18.018 --> 00:01:23.724
Trusted proxy settings should match the
real infrastructure because they influence

20
00:01:23.804 --> 00:01:29.272
how the application interprets client IPs,
protocols, and secure request state.

21
00:01:29.352 --> 00:01:33.869
HTTPS enforcement, cookie Secure behavior,
redirect generation,

22
00:01:33.949 --> 00:01:36.565
health endpoints, metrics endpoints,

23
00:01:36.645 --> 00:01:41.954
and documentation routes should all be
reviewed in the deployed architecture,

24
00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:43.540
not only on localhost.
